Milestone 1 Phase D - backlight PWM and brightness validation
Waveshare ESP32-S3-LCD-2.8 (SKU 30223, non-touch) - 2026-08-03

Captured from the native USB Serial/JTAG console at 115200 baud.
Firmware: hardware-validation profile, git 55bfa891b3d5, dirty=true
(Phase D work uncommitted at capture time).

Normalisation applied to this file, and nothing else:
  - ANSI colour escapes removed
  - CR removed and trailing whitespace stripped, so the file is LF-only
  - ESP-IDF Verbose-level lines (prefix 'V') dropped: SPI bus-lock and
    polling-transaction plumbing that repeats hundreds of times per pass.
    Debug, Info, Warning and Error levels are kept in full.

The unfiltered captures were scanned for faults before filtering:
0 Guru Meditation, 0 panic, 0 backtrace, 0 stack overflow, 0 assert,
0 watchdog, 0 FAILED draw or re-time. Raw captures kept outside the
repository alongside the other Phase B/C/D artefacts.

==============================================================================
PART 1 - brightness step walk and fades at 5 kHz
flow: CONFIG_PRD_DISPLAY_BRIGHTNESS_TEST

Steps carry an on-screen marker count so a dark-room observer can name the
step: 1=off 2=1% 3=2% 4=3% 5=4% 6=5% 7=10% 8=25% 9=50% 10=75% 11=100%
